<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3064" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpollŏdōrus</span></b> ,
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπολλοδωρος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A distinguished rhetorician</i>, <i>teacher of Augustus</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 89</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. Or.
			19</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpollŏdōrēi</span></b> ,
				<i>his pupils</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 2,
				11, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 1,
				18 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A distinguished grammarian of Athens</i>, <i>author of a work on mythology still extant</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Att. 12, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>An Academic philosopher</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				1, 34, 93</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A tyrant of Cassandrea</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 33, 82</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
